{"nodes": [{"id": "markdown_arch_tui_app_design_app", "label": "primeparts TUI application design (screens, presets, dispatch)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "markdown/arch/tui_app_design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "markdown_arch_tui_app_design_field_dispatch", "label": "Schema-field-name value dispatch (the 'c' key, accept-sets)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/arch/tui_app_design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Dispatch is purely schema-field-name based (no type/domain abstraction); each query declares a literal accept-set of field names, so a q_k cell can feed p-lookup because both are prime columns."}, {"id": "markdown_arch_tui_app_design_p_pushdown", "label": "p-scan window as predicate pushdown on p", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/arch/tui_app_design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Value is exact (k==K); the [p_lo,p_hi] range is a pushdown And(Equal(k,K),GtEq(p,p_lo),LtEq(p,p_hi)) that bounds the scan \u2014 load-bearing because there is no max_k stat to prune on, so k=16 needs the window or scans to EOF."}, {"id": "markdown_arch_tui_app_design_cancellable", "label": "Cancellable, progress-tracked, threaded execution", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "markdown/arch/tui_app_design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "markdown_arch_tui_app_design_app", "target": "markdown_arch_tui_app_design_field_dispatch", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "markdown/arch/tui_app_design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "markdown_arch_tui_app_design_app", "target": "markdown_arch_tui_ap